  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Choose between process and state",
   "texto": [
    "**Werden + Partizip II** focuses the event: **Der Patient wird operiert** (they operate on the patient / are being operated). **Sein + Partizip II** focuses the resulting state: **Der Patient ist operiert** (the patient is already in operation). The context, not just the form, decides whether the process passive is translated with «se» or «is being»."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Identify time",
   "texto": [
    "**Der Patient wurde operiert** is Präteritum of the process passive (it was operated / operated). **Der Patient ist operiert worden** is Perfekt of that passive. On the other hand, **Der Patient ist operiert** describes the current state. They are not interchangeable forms: see **worden** and the situation described."
   ]
  },
